Changes with PassiveDNS 1.3.0

- Add -s for the live snapshot length and raise the default from 1600 to 4096
- Move the SIGUSR1 stats file option from -s to --stats-file
- Warn when generic-receive-offload is enabled on the capture device
- Print the snapshot length and enabled record letters at startup unless -q
- Document the Ubuntu 26.04 build and drop the older distro notes
- Tell the test runner when the passivedns binary is missing
- Build with PIE, full RELRO, a non-executable stack, and fortified libc calls
- Log HTTPS and SVCB answers by default
- Log an empty NOERROR answer when -X 0 is set
- Add -f i for the IP TTL, or IPv6 hop limit, of the reply
- Extend copyright notices through 2026
- Apply a requested user, group, or chroot when reading a pcap with -r
- Exit with an error when -r cannot open the pcap
- Do not accept a DNS answer whose id was not stored from a query, including id 0
- Restore the full field and RR-type mask when -f or -X has no valid flag
- Add regression tests for the decoder, the command line, and the Perl tools

Changes with PassiveDNS 1.2.2

- Reject short, wrapped, and zero-length IP headers before parsing
- Stop IP-in-IP recursion and walk IPv6 extension headers
- Reassemble IPv4 and IPv6 fragments, and DNS messages over TCP
- Format log lines on the heap with a hard length cap
- Copy DNS record type, class, and TTL so a freed packet is not reused
- Cap live flows and count strings, flows, and reassembly buffers
- Fail closed when a requested user, group, or chroot cannot be applied
- Hold the pid file open so its lock stays
- Create log files mode 0640
- Read database credentials from the environment in the Perl and PHP tools
- Send SQL through placeholders, and escape HTML in the local demo page
- Build with -fstack-protector-strong when using GCC

Changes with PassiveDNS 1.2.0

- Added enhancements to better handle high volume traffic
- Added support for LOC records
- Added support for DNSSEC records
- Added support for HINFO records
- Added support for SPF records
- Added support for SSHFP records
- Support for DLT_RAW pcap files
- Added support for LINKTYPE_LINUX_SLL
- Added autotools support
- Better OSX support
- Added pf_ring support
- Added support for SIGHUP to reopen log files
- Added support for JSON output
- Added syslog output option
- Added support for expire_all_dns_records on SIGUSR2

Changes with PassiveDNS 1.1.3

- Added a fix for correct CNAME handling
- Makefile improvements

Changes with PassiveDNS 1.1.2

- Zero padding to microseconds
- Added a simple webui in php for searching the pdns mysql db.

Changes with PassiveDNS 1.1.1

- Added stats output to stdout with SIGUSR1 signal
- Added support for more Server Return Codes

Changes with PassiveDNS 1.0.0

- Added microseconds to unix timestamps in log output
- Added "count" field in log output.
- Added more stat fields when exiting

Changes with PassiveDNS 0.5.1

- Fixed an issue of lost dns_records (memleak and finally a cpu spinn)
- Fixed segfault when unable to read pcap
- Fixed segfault when packet payload was only one byte

Changes with PassiveDNS 0.5.0

- Cleaned up unused code

Changes with PassiveDNS 0.3.4

- Added NXDOMAIN support
